{"id":27551,"slug":"the-mikado","title":"The Mikado","year":1939,"country":"United Kingdom, United States","duration":91,"spine":559,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27551-the-mikado","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/e3c058a69006d26b6df4008dcbc87616/m2TegG4mLAOkV3oQmmKYYZxQmuFF8b_large.jpg","description":"The legendary Gilbert and Sullivan troupe the D’Oyly Carte Opera Company joined forces with Hollywood for this 1939 Technicolor version of the beloved comic opera The Mikado, the first work by the famed duo to be adapted for the screen. Directed by musician and Oscar-nominated filmmaker Victor Schertzinger, it is a lavish cinematic retelling of the British political satire set in exotic Japan, with such enduringly popular numbers as “A Wand’ring Minstrel I” and “Three Little Maids from School,” and featuring American singer Kenny Baker as well as a host of renowned D’Oyly Carte performers, including Martyn Green and Sydney Granville.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Victor Schertzinger","slug":"victor-schertzinger"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Kenny Baker","role":"Nanki-Poo","slug":"kenny-baker"},{"actor":"Martyn Green","role":"Ko-Ko","slug":"martyn-green"},{"actor":"Sydney Granville","role":"Pooh-Bah","slug":"sydney-granville"},{"actor":"John Barclay","role":"The Mikado","slug":"john-barclay"},{"actor":"Gregory Stroud","role":"Pish-Tush","slug":"gregory-stroud"},{"actor":"Jean Colin","role":"Yum-Yum","slug":"jean-colin"},{"actor":"Constance Willis","role":"Katisha","slug":"constance-willis"},{"actor":"Elizabeth Paynter","role":"Pitti-Sing","slug":"elizabeth-paynter"},{"actor":"Kathleen Naylor","role":"Peep-Bo","slug":"kathleen-naylor"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Victor Schertzinger","slug":"victor-schertzinger"},{"role":"Based upon the opera by","person":"W. S. Gilbert and Arthur Sullivan","slug":null},{"role":"By arrangement with","person":"Rupert D’Oyly Carte","slug":null},{"role":"Adapted, conducted, and produ